Break and Continue in JavaBreak and Continue are both used to control the flow of loops, each in its way. The break statement stops the loop entirely, while the continue statement skips the current iteration and proceeds with the next, allowing the rest of the loop to function as usual.Example:
            Java

    // Java Program to implement continue
// And break in same loop
import java.io.*;

class Geeks
{
    public static void main(String[] args)
    {
        for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) 
        {
          	// Skip condition where i==3
            if (i == 3) 
                continue;

          	// Exit the loop when i == 7
            if (i == 7) 
                break; 

            System.out.print(i + " ");
        }
    }
}

